# Verbatim excerpts from the main 90+ minute soak run's app.log (PID 206161, boot ~2026-08-30
# 22:36:40 local / 14:36:40 UTC).
#
# NOTE - operator error: the full raw app.log for this run (~4900 lines) was deleted by
# `rm -f run/logs/app.log` immediately before the post-SIGTERM restart, before it was archived.
# That was a mistake - it should have been renamed, not removed. samples.csv and events.log
# were never touched and are complete for the whole run. The excerpts below are exact copies
# captured directly from the live log during the run, before the deletion, while investigating
# each injection; they are not reconstructed or paraphrased. Timestamps in the log are in the
# process's local timezone (UTC+8); events.log and samples.csv use UTC.

## Injection 1 - Oracle partition (docker pause 14:59:02Z .. unpause 15:02:13Z UTC)
# The refresh that was in flight when Oracle was paused blocked for the full pause duration
# (no error, no SOURCE_ERROR - the 3-minute pause never reached the 300s query-timeout-seconds
# ceiling) and completed the moment Oracle came back:
2026-08-30 23:02:12,955 INFO  [etl.JdbcGenerationSource] (executor-thread-22) group equipment generation 69: 40 row(s) read into equipment, dataAsOf 2026-08-30T14:59:16.930869914Z
2026-08-30 23:02:13,168 INFO  [etl.JdbcGenerationSource] (executor-thread-22) group wip generation 69: 500 row(s) read into wip, dataAsOf 2026-08-30T15:02:13.052187316Z
# (dataAsOf for equipment gen 69 is 14:59:16 - the query STARTED right as the pause began, and
# the log line for its completion is timestamped 15:02:12/13, ~3 minutes later, i.e. it landed
# the instant the container was unpaused. samples.csv shows the matching signature: current
# generation frozen at 68 and live_generations at 2.0 (a stuck in-flight candidate) for the
# entire pause window, snapping to 70 and back to live=1.0 within one sample after unpause.)

