## Injection 3 - concurrent task trigger (15:39:00Z .. 15:39:48Z UTC)
# curl -X POST .../admin/etl/tasks/wip-summary/runs, /equipment-uptime/runs, /wip-summary-concurrent/runs
wip:403 equipment:403 wip2:403
# Same auth gap. The soak's cron-native substitute - wip-summary and wip-summary-concurrent
# share cron "0/15 * * * * ?" and have fired in the same scheduler tick on every cycle since
# boot, both against the same report.db target via independent JDBC connections:
2026-08-30 23:39:15,905 INFO  [inf.etl.tas.TaskEngine] (DefaultDispatcher-worker-5 @wip-summary#752) run 0ea2a3af-52cf-4edb-a178-26032190a4b7 task wip-summary step copy-wip: copied 500 rows from cache wip group wip, generation 180 as of 2026-08-30T15:38:56.998039396Z into scratch dataset wip_cache
2026-08-30 23:39:15,902 INFO  [etl.run] (DefaultDispatcher-worker-4 @wip-summary-concurrent#751) run 8d8eed34-63bb-4e4a-8604-c7000a7845eb step load/summarise ok: 0 read, 0 written, 13 ms, attempt 1
2026-08-30 23:39:15,974 INFO  [etl.run] (DefaultDispatcher-worker-5 @wip-summary#752) run 0ea2a3af-52cf-4edb-a178-26032190a4b7 step load/publish ok: 2 read, 2 written, 55 ms, attempt 1
2026-08-30 23:39:16,001 INFO  [etl.run] (DefaultDispatcher-worker-4 @wip-summary-concurrent#751) run 8d8eed34-63bb-4e4a-8604-c7000a7845eb step load/publish ok: 2 read, 2 written, 99 ms, attempt 1
2026-08-30 23:39:16,049 INFO  [etl.run] (DefaultDispatcher-worker-5 @wip-summary#752) run 0ea2a3af-52cf-4edb-a178-26032190a4b7 task wip-summary ended SUCCEEDED
2026-08-30 23:39:16,076 INFO  [etl.run] (DefaultDispatcher-worker-4 @wip-summary-concurrent#751) run 8d8eed34-63bb-4e4a-8604-c7000a7845eb task wip-summary-concurrent ended SUCCEEDED
# Every one of ~180+ such concurrent pairs over the run SUCCEEDED - no DuckDB file-lock
# contention observed (Producers.kt's KDoc warns about *cross-process* contention on one
# DuckDB file; two connections from within the same JVM process share the embedded instance
# and did not collide).

## Unplanned finding - one checkpoint I/O failure, self-healed (~15:24:57Z UTC, T+46min,
## unrelated to any scheduled injection - found only because the soak ran long enough)
2026-08-30 23:24:57,338 WARN  [inf.sna.duc.DuckDbGenerationStore] (executor-thread-49) CHECKPOINT of candidate 138 failed: FATAL Error: Failed to create checkpoint because of error: Could not write file "/mnt/c/Users/maxch/OneDrive/.../soak/run/state/cache/wip/gen_0000000138.db.tmp": Cannot allocate memory
2026-08-30 23:24:57,546 WARN  [inf.sna.cor.RefreshCycle] (executor-thread-49) Verify rejected candidate generation 138 of group wip: rule=key_unique detail=counting ids of table wip: IO Error: Corrupt database file: computed checksum 5381 does not match stored checksum 0 in block at location 274432
# Occurred exactly once in ~270 refresh cycles x 2 groups (~540 checkpoint attempts). The next
# refresh cycle (generation 139) succeeded normally, readiness never dropped (samples.csv shows
# ready/200 continuously through this window), and no gen_0000000138.db / .tmp / .wal file was
# left on disk afterward - the framework's verify gate rejected the corrupt candidate rather
# than publishing it, exactly the safety property spec 10.1's verify step exists for.

## Injection 4 - SIGTERM (16:09:36Z UTC)
2026-08-30 23:09:34,959 INFO  [etl.run] (DefaultDispatcher-worker-5 @equipment-uptime#1116) run f7301477-c748-4ab4-8514-afe3a56ac31b task equipment-uptime ended SUCCEEDED
2026-08-30 23:09:36,635 INFO  [io.quarkus] (Shutdown thread) etl-host stopped in 0.337s
# Process (PID 206161) disappeared from /proc within the ~1s polling granularity used; no
# WARN/ERROR logged during shutdown (EtlHost.onStop only logs on wired.close()/managed.close()
# *failure*, so silence here is the expected clean-shutdown signature). Exact process exit code
# was not captured: the process was started via nohup+disown for durability across tool calls,
# so it was reparented to WSL's init and was not a child of the shell that sent the SIGTERM or
# polled for exit - its exit status is therefore only visible to that init process, which this
# soak did not instrument. Reported as not-captured rather than guessed.

